<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Four Garrisons of Anxi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">648–c. 790</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Four Garrisons of Anxi were <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang dynasty</a> military posts in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tarim-basin">Tarim Basin</a>, usually Kucha, Khotan, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kashgar">Kashgar</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karashahr">Karasahr</a>, under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anxi-protectorate">Protectorate General to Pacify the West</a>. They secured Chinese control of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk-road">Silk Road</a> oasis kingdoms, which kept their own rulers, and were repeatedly contested with the Tibetan Empire, which took them around 790.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/four-garrisons-of-anxi.jpg" alt="Four Garrisons of Anxi" width="320" height="210" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Yug · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Emperor_Taizong%27s_campaign_against_Xiyu_states.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
